# bewae cron jobs — paste into the Pi user's crontab via `crontab -e`
#
# Schedule:
#   06:00, 18:00  →  calculate_weather_multiplier.py  (OWM forecast → wm)
#   06:05, 18:05  →  check_soil_moisture.py           (sets wm=0 if soil already wet)
#
# The 5-minute gap matters: the moisture check must run AFTER the weather
# multiplier so it can override wm to 0 when the soil is already wet.
#
# Assumptions:
#   - Scripts live in /home/pi/bewae/  (matches monitoring_config.JSON → config_path)
#   - python3 is on cron's default PATH; if not, replace with /usr/bin/python3
#   - Run as the `pi` user (NOT root) so file ownership matches the rest of the install
#   - Remote logging goes to LogFire; local cron.log is a fallback for when the Pi
#     can't reach Node-RED (boot, network outage). Tail with `tail -f ~/bewae/cron.log`.
#
# Verify after install with:  crontab -l

0  6  * * *  cd /home/pi/bewae && python3 calculate_weather_multiplier.py >> /home/pi/bewae/cron.log 2>&1
0 18  * * *  cd /home/pi/bewae && python3 calculate_weather_multiplier.py >> /home/pi/bewae/cron.log 2>&1
5  6  * * *  cd /home/pi/bewae && python3 check_soil_moisture.py          >> /home/pi/bewae/cron.log 2>&1
5 18  * * *  cd /home/pi/bewae && python3 check_soil_moisture.py          >> /home/pi/bewae/cron.log 2>&1
